      "math_academy_id": "q-148034",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [0,2],$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{2}y(4x+3y).\n$$\n\nFind ${F}_{X}(x),$ the marginal CDF of $X,$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=F(x,\\infty )={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }F(x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $0\\le x\\le 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & =F(x,\\infty ) \\\\  & =F(x,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{2}(2)(4x+3(2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{2}(4x+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
